<title>GERMANY: Lufthansa adds flights due to BA strike.</title>
<headline>Lufthansa adds flights due to BA strike.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-07-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lufthansa AG said on Wednesday it was offering additional flights and using larger aircraft on existing flights due to a strike by cabin crew at British Airways.</p>
<p>The German carrier said it would offer three additional flights to London on Wednesday and Thursday, raising its daily offering to nine flights from Frankfurt to London.</p>
<p>Lufthansa also said it was using larger aircraft on flights between London and Berlin and Hamburg due to the strike.</p>
<p>Striking cabin crew forced BA to cancel half its flights out of London on Wednesday, leaving 25,000 passengers stranded.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
